    "title": "Selena Gomez and Olivia Rodrigo Just Declared a Girly New Color Trend for Spring",
    "text": "2 min readTHE RUNDOWNBoth Selena Gomez and Olivia Rodrigo wore girly pink minidresses with contrasting white accents yesterday.Rodrigo had on a Peter Pan-collared dress for her third album’s cover art.Gomez, meanwhile, chose a satin-pink Prada minidress for Rare Beauty’s event that evening.Just hours after Olivia Rodrigo released the cover art for her third album, which featured her in a pink Peter Pan-collared minidress, Selena Gomez went out in her own girly pink look from Prada’s spring 2026 collection. The Rare Beauty founder stepped out for her brand’s True To Myself Natural Matte Longwear Foundation L.A. launch event, wearing a satin minidress with a white embellished neckline. She accessorized with hoop earrings and white heels.Stefanie Keenan//Getty ImagesAdvertisement - Continue Reading BelowStefanie Keenan//Getty ImagesRodrigo’s dress also had contrasting white accents with its folded sleeves and bold collar. Fans noted it was similar to the dress she wore on Saturday Night Live in 2023:Advertisement - Continue Reading BelowNBC//Getty ImagesThis isn’t Rodrigo’s first pink minidress of the season, either. She wore a more formal pale-pink look from Saint Laurent by Anthony Vaccarello to the Vanity Fair Oscar Party last month:Lionel Hahn//Getty ImagesWhile minidresses are a staple for celebrities in warmer weather, Rodrigo and Gomez’s matching pink moment hints at the color having a girly comeback this spring. Last year, a paler version of the hue—ballet pink—was on the rise as fashion lovers embraced balletcore.Gomez’s appearance comes weeks after she spoke to People about her current beauty era, describing it as “classic, maybe a little sexy. I feel flirty,” she said. “I still feel young, I think. I like a little flirty, classic look.”She also reflected on her broader career plans, telling the outlet that she feels empowered when she’s “doing work within my community. I think that’s the best part is being able to connect with people and that’s what I’m so excited about. This next era will be very much me just embracing everyone, hopefully.”Advertisement - Continue Reading BelowHer beauty brand’s newly launched matte foundation was literally years in the making. Rare Beauty shared photos of Gomez testing the product not just during her September 2025 wedding but also as far back as April 2024 during her NBA game date with Benny Blanco:Sarah Stier//Getty Images",
